**PASS.** I loaded the current build cold at http://localhost:8000 and watched it start. Loading and startup work, and I found no fault to send to a coder.

**Which build I tested:** HEAD e500c44 plus uncommitted changes (diff hash 441e441a…). Every file in `dist/` is identical to the build the previous site review (lFGon0) passed. `dist/` is up to date with the source, so I didn't rebuild. Nothing was running on port 8000, so I started my own server there and stopped only that one at the end.

**What I saw in Chromium:**
- **Loading:** the page, all scripts, the WASM and the game data loaded with status 200 and the right file types. No requests failed and there were no page or console errors.
- **First frame:** the engine was running and drawing within 206 ms, well inside the 2 s target. The title screen colours are correct, with no red/blue swap.
- **Speed:** the game runs at 35 tics per second, which is Doom's normal rate. The page never froze for longer than about 10 ms.
- **Menu:** Escape opens and closes the main menu, and the demo keeps running behind it, as in the original.
- **Layout:** the picture keeps its 16:10 shape with no scrollbars at both 1280x720 and 800x600.
- **Two things that look odd but are normal:**
  - One screenshot has a red tint. It's the game's damage flash: health drops from 83% to 65% in the demo between the two shots.
  - The console shows two warnings that audio can't start before the user clicks. That's Chrome's autoplay rule.

**Still open, none of it about startup:**
- **Tester, carried over:** the expected results in `faults.sh` are overstated, and the stall and speed checks need to allow for the ~1.1 s screen-wipe freeze. I didn't re-check either this run.
- **Needs a person:** Firefox, Safari, high-DPI screens, listening to the audio, and a real hidden tab haven't been tested.

The pass criteria are ones the agents proposed; you haven't approved them. "Cold" means I cleared the cache in the shared test browser rather than using a fresh profile. I didn't change any source, test or build files.

